{"title":"2013 CEMC Cayley Problems/Problem 23","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2013_CEMC_Cayley_Problems/Problem_23&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>One bag contains <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/c/41c544263a265ff15498ee45f7392c5f86c6d151.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> red marbles and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/c/41c544263a265ff15498ee45f7392c5f86c6d151.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> blue marbles. A second bag contains <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/c/41c544263a265ff15498ee45f7392c5f86c6d151.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> red marbles, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/c/41c544263a265ff15498ee45f7392c5f86c6d151.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> blue marbles, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/1/1/311cabda3a9b09f0dde217303ca9d1cd9201dcf6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$g$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" /> green marbles, with <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/0/b/10b9b67f8a2f73e574a0256b793b1a194ce5cd75.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$g &gt; 0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"44\" height=\"17\" />. For each bag, Maria calculates the probability of randomly drawing two marbles of the same colour in two draws from that bag, without replacement. (Drawing two marbles <i>without replacement</i> means drawing two marbles, one after the other, without putting the first marble back into the bag.) If these two probabilities are equal, then the value of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/1/1/311cabda3a9b09f0dde217303ca9d1cd9201dcf6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$g$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" /> is \n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/c/0/3c0673652e5f6a8460708773e268586583e71609.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(A)}\\   4  \\qquad \t\\textbf{(B)}\\   5  \\qquad \t\\textbf{(C)}\\   6  \\qquad \t\\textbf{(D)}\\   7  \\qquad \t\\textbf{(E)}\\   8  \\qquad$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"384\" height=\"18\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution\">Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2013_CEMC_Cayley_Problems/Problem_23&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>For the first bag, we want to calculate the probability of either drawing two red marbles or two blue marbles.\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/0/2/302a6e89035f3c6ab3b83e5857160f9fc9899c40.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[P(\\text{Two Same Color in 1st Bag}) = P(RR) + P(BB) = \\frac{2}{4} \\cdot \\frac{1}{3} + \\frac{2}{4} \\cdot \\frac{1}{3} = \\frac{1}{3}.\\]\" width=\"538\" height=\"37\" />\n</p><p>Similarly, for the second bag,\n\\begin{align}\n\tP(\\text{Two Same Color in 2nd Bag}) &amp;= P(RR) + P(BB) + P(GG)\\\\\n\t&amp;= \\frac{2}{4+g} \\cdot \\frac{1}{3+g} + \\frac{2}{4+g} \\cdot \\frac{1}{3+g} + \\frac{g}{4+g} \\cdot \\frac{g-1}{3+g}\\\\\n\t&amp;= \\frac{g^2-g+4}{g^2+7g+12}.\n\\end{align}\nWe are given that these two probabilities are equal, so\n\\begin{align}\n\t\\frac{1}{3} &amp;= \\frac{g^2 - g + 4}{g^2 + 7g + 12}\\\\\n\tg^2 + 7g + 12 &amp;= 3g^2 - 3g + 12 \\\\\n\t0 &amp;= 2g^2 - 10g \\\\\n\t0 &amp;= 2g(g-5), \\\\\n\\end{align}\nwhence either <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/a/e/9aed69e8cdc7248553fa2017ba6426a12a132905.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$g=0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"44\" height=\"17\" /> or <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/0/4/b0447205c6df910f15ca840c7b2b16057f292970.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$g=5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"44\" height=\"17\" />. But we are given that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/e/3/9e3849c5b7c821dacfcedd9e2890150a511b69bb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$g&gt;0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"44\" height=\"17\" />, so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/2/3/5235d93dafa71e6c0d6972b8ee347da9e020e2c1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$g = \\boxed{\\textbf{(B)}\\   5}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"90\" height=\"30\" />.\n</p><p>~Blosp\n</p>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2013_CEMC_Cayley\" title=\"2013 CEMC Cayley\">2013 CEMC Cayley</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2013_CEMC_Cayley_Problems\" title=\"2013 CEMC Cayley Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2013_CEMC_Cayley_Answer_Key&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2013 CEMC Cayley Answer Key (page does not exist)\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://cemc.math.uwaterloo.ca/contests/past_contests.html\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2013_CEMC_Cayley_Problems/Problem_22\" title=\"2013 CEMC Cayley Problems/Problem 22\">Problem 22</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2013_CEMC_Cayley_Problems/Problem_24&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2013 CEMC Cayley Problems/Problem 24 (page does not exist)\">Problem 24</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2013_CEMC_Cayley_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"2013 CEMC Cayley Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2013_CEMC_Cayley_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"2013 CEMC Cayley Problems/Problem 2\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2013_CEMC_Cayley_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"2013 CEMC Cayley Problems/Problem 3\">3</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2013_CEMC_Cayley_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"2013 CEMC Cayley Problems/Problem 4\">4</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2013_CEMC_Cayley_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"2013 CEMC Cayley Problems/Problem 5\">5</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2013_CEMC_Cayley_Problems/Problem_6\" title=\"2013 CEMC Cayley Problems/Problem 6\">6</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2013_CEMC_Cayley_Problems/Problem_7\" title=\"2013 CEMC Cayley Problems/Problem 7\">7</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2013_CEMC_Cayley_Problems/Problem_8\" title=\"2013 CEMC Cayley Problems/Problem 8\">8</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2013_CEMC_Cayley_Problems/Problem_9\" title=\"2013 CEMC Cayley Problems/Problem 9\">9</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2013_CEMC_Cayley_Problems/Problem_10\" title=\"2013 CEMC Cayley Problems/Problem 10\">10</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2013_CEMC_Cayley_Problems/Problem_11\" title=\"2013 CEMC Cayley Problems/Problem 11\">11</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2013_CEMC_Cayley_Problems/Problem_12\" title=\"2013 CEMC Cayley Problems/Problem 12\">12</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2013_CEMC_Cayley_Problems/Problem_13\" title=\"2013 CEMC Cayley Problems/Problem 13\">13</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2013_CEMC_Cayley_Problems/Problem_14\" title=\"2013 CEMC Cayley Problems/Problem 14\">14</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2013_CEMC_Cayley_Problems/Problem_15\" tit